[list] ["Sign-in providers","You are working on the installation. 60 minutes left.","The ways in this installation offers every workspace on it. Offered is not on: each workspace's owner decides whether to take one - except where the installation's ways to sign in are locked with providers among them, which turns on every provider that admits only invited people. Each row says which applies.","Offer a provider","This installation offers no provider of its own. Every workspace configures its own, or none.","Offer a provider","Cancel","Hubtask fetches the issuer's metadata before storing anything, so an address that cannot be reached is refused here rather than by the first person who tries to sign in.","Which provider","Google","Microsoft","Another provider","Offered to every workspace, a provider without a directory lets in only the people each workspace invited. Anyone else it knows is turned away.","Register Hubtask as a confidential client that supports the authorization code flow with PKCE, and add the redirect address below as its redirect URI. Hubtask asks for the openid, email and profile scopes and reads the issuer's discovery document, so anything that publishes one works - Keycloak, Authentik, Okta, Zitadel, Auth0, GitLab, a directory of your own. Where to look, by name: Keycloak calls it Clients, with Client authentication on and Standard flow enabled, and the issuer is your realm's address. Authentik calls it Providers, OAuth2/OpenID, Confidential. Okta calls it Applications, Web Application. Zitadel calls it Applications, Web, Code with PKCE. Auth0 calls it Applications, Regular Web Application. Two things that are not obvious. The issuer is the address whose discovery document names itself - not the sign-in page, and usually not the address you registered at; paste it and Hubtask fetches it before saving, so a wrong one is refused here rather than by the first person who tries. And Hubtask cannot tell whether this provider verifies the addresses it hands out, so an account that already exists here is connected to it only after that account's own password. Invited people accept their invitation through this provider from their invitation's own link - choosing the provider on the sign-in page instead is refused, because Hubtask cannot tell whether this provider runs their mailbox.","Redirect address","http://hubtask.localhost:18540/auth/callback","Enter it at the provider exactly as shown.","Copy the address","Issuer*","The https address the provider identifies itself by. Every token must name it exactly.","Client id*","Client secret","Sealed when it is saved and never answered again.","Name on the button","Left empty it is the issuer's host, which is where the button sends people anyway.","Who this provider may admit","Only people invited here","Only what this provider is allowed to do is offered here. What a preset forbids is not a choice somebody can make and then have refused.","Position","The order the buttons are drawn in, lowest first.","Cancel","Save the provider"]

